I'd be a bit reluctant to do this; pets need to
forage or they'll starve. One of the things on which
they feed is peaceful monsters, and peaceful
monsters don't tend to migrate toward you, and thus
not toward a pet confined near you, so your pet
needs to be free to go find the peacefuls.

> 2) Drop a cursed dart on the piled shop
> merchandise in the far corner,

This is _really_ a good idea, since if you keep the
cursed item on top, your pet absolutely won't _pick
up_ the top item, and thus not any of them, though it
may still eat a tripe ration (or other appropriate
treat) out from under a cursed item, greedy little
snarfler that it is. If you can "Elbereth" under the
stack, (most?) hostiles that pop up when you step
out the shop door won't loot the stack either. That
still, IIUC, leaves it vulnerable to suddenly popped
up peacefuls, though.

